From e71aae0edde214ad187ed42dced014cf2a0d19e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 13:36:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 00/45] ours base for r209: moe-expert-cache.cu stays at r206
 (r207 host-pool-speed not carried, pool mode at r206)

r207-r209 rewrote the host pool path of moe-expert-cache.cu (pool-tier gather, per-table pool sizing,
the MOE_HOST_POOL_RAM_PCT ceiling, the report snapshot).  It overlaps code our series replaces (the next
patch removes the #266 remap and pool cold; the mmap / L2 work changes the bounce and gather paths), and
production runs --host-experts mmap.  Keep the r206 file and answer moe_cache_table_is_pool with false, so
the new scheduler default (gather pool-backed tables only) never gathers: the r206 behaviour.
